  "Optional. Without it ORIX Clean still works on everything macOS lets it read, and tells you what was not read. With it, protected folders (Mail, Safari data, the Trash, other apps' containers) are included. It never gives access to system files protected by System Integrity Protection, and ORIX Clean never asks for an administrator password.": {
   "localizations": {
    "en": {
     "stringUnit": {
      "state": "translated",
      "value": "Optional. Without it ORIX Clean still works on everything macOS lets it read, and tells you what was not read. With it, protected folders (Mail, Safari data, the Trash, other apps' containers) are included. It never gives access to system files protected by System Integrity Protection, and ORIX Clean never asks for an administrator password."
     }
    },
    "fr-CA": {
     "stringUnit": {
      "state": "translated",
      "value": "Facultatif. Sans lui, ORIX Clean fonctionne quand même sur tout ce que macOS le laisse lire, et vous indique ce qui n’a pas été lu. Avec lui, les dossiers protégés (Mail, données de Safari, Corbeille, conteneurs d’autres apps) sont inclus. Il ne donne jamais accès aux fichiers système protégés par la Protection de l’intégrité du système, et ORIX Clean ne demande jamais de mot de passe d’administrateur."
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "Other": {
   "localizations": {
    "en": {
